  "question": {
    "text": "<p>One mole of an ideal monoatomic gas undergoes two reversible processes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> as shown in the given figure:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0005_1a5ad1f42899.png\" style=\"width: 420px; height: 351px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> is an adiabatic process. If the total heat absorbed in the entire process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>RT</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>ln</mi><mn>10</mn></math>,&nbsp;the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>logV</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is<br />[Use molar heat capacity of the gas at constant pressure, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>]</p>"
  },
